    "reasoning": "q-73602: Eliminating t gives y=2-(x+1)^2/4 with -7≤x≤5, a downward-opening parabola with vertex (-1,2) and endpoints (-7,-7) and (5,-7). Current option 1 matches this parabola; the source plot adds sampled-point markers. q-123785: Adding the equations gives x+y=2. As t increases from 0 to 3, the curve traces the line segment from (5,-3) to (-4,6), matching current option 4. Its source plot shows the same segment with sampled-point markers. The source image paths are preserved separately in ma_value. q-125968: This geometric series has ratio -2/e, whose absolute value is less than 1, so its sum is 1/(1+2/e)=e/(e+2), matching option 3 and the source conclusion. q-170524: Comparing with the standard rotation matrix gives cos(θ)=1/2 and sin(θ)=-√3/2, hence θ=-π/3, a clockwise rotation by π/3, matching option 0 and the source conclusion. All four mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions.",
